From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:12:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] conn: let an embedder register an additional control
 function

Socket options applied in listenConfig() are the only ones guaranteed to
survive a rebind, since Device.BindUpdate() closes and reopens the sockets on
every listen_port change. An embedder that needs per-descriptor treatment --
on Android, VpnService.protect(), without which the tunnel's own packets are
routed back into the tunnel -- currently has to re-apply it after the fact and
race the rebind. Add AddControlFn so it can be applied before bind instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PVGaNeNhqp11rTLwZ9rM4J
---
 conn/controlfns.go | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/conn/controlfns.go b/conn/controlfns.go
index 27421bd..1432ef6 100644
--- a/conn/controlfns.go
+++ b/conn/controlfns.go
@@ -26,6 +26,18 @@ type controlFn func(network, address string, c syscall.RawConn) error
 // that can apply socket options.
 var controlFns = []controlFn{}
 
+// AddControlFn registers an additional function to run against every socket
+// before it is bound, after the platform defaults. It lets an embedder apply
+// per-socket configuration that must hold across rebinds -- on Android,
+// VpnService.protect(), which is per descriptor and therefore lost whenever a
+// listen_port change makes the device reopen its sockets.
+//
+// It must be called before the device is brought up and is not safe to call
+// concurrently with Bind.Open.
+func AddControlFn(fn func(network, address string, c syscall.RawConn) error) {
+	controlFns = append(controlFns, fn)
+}
+
 // listenConfig returns a net.ListenConfig that applies the controlFns to the
 // socket prior to bind. This is used to apply socket buffer sizing and packet
 // information OOB configuration for sticky sockets.
